plc/new-mexico/valencia-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids March to April came in under 90% of normal in 41 of them. In 2025, January to February ran 17% and February to March 15% of normal on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 8% of normal there. Every grid had its driest year in 1956, and grid 17493 fell to 29% that year.</p>"}
